d #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202610/fork_wait_session_turn_target.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-1q4[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-1q4/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Promotion-aware bare-name fork waits[/bold #D7AFFF]                          [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]promotion[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]promotion: bind bare-name forks as session seeds, heal queued legacy [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]kind=agent records whose parent was promoted, keep exact members [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]single-turn, pin the 16h replay and continuation regressions.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Rust wait-target vocabulary and pure rules[/bold #D7AFFF]                    [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]vocab[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]vocab: add sase-core wait_target module (parse, effective-target rules, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]current-turn selection), the wait_target NamedEnum, pyo3 bindings, and a[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]thin Python facade.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Keyword-only macro inputs in sase-core[/bold #D7AFFF]                        [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]kwonly_core[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]kwonly_core: add keyword_only to the Rust macro input contract (catalog,[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]wires, frontmatter rules, positional mapping, signatures, gateway [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]contract).[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Turn-pinned wait records and evaluation[/bold #D7AFFF]                       [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]wait_runtime[dim] · [dim][/dim]after promotion, vocab[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]wait_runtime: add the shared Python binder that pins a session's current[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]turn into v2 identity records, evaluate turn-scoped records, and keep [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]persistence, member dirs, and confirmation consistent.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]The %wait target= keyword end to end[/bold #D7AFFF]                          [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]wait_directive[dim] · [dim][/dim]after wait_runtime[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]wait_directive: accept and validate %wait(..., target=) in the Python [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]collector and Rust editor/typed parsers, feed the binder, round-trip it [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]through PromptWaitDirective edits, and update docs.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]sase agent wait --target[/bold #D7AFFF]                                      [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]agent_wait_cli[dim] · [dim][/dim]after wait_runtime[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]agent_wait_cli: add -T/--target session|turn to sase agent wait, using [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the shared binder to wait on one pinned turn.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  7 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Turn targets in plan-gate coder options[/bold #D7AFFF]                       [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]coder_options[dim] · [dim][/dim]after wait_directive[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]coder_options: add turn=<agent> to the wait-spec grammar and carry it [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]through the approval response, gateless approve, coder prompts, and epic[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]launches as %wait(..., target=turn).[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  8 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Show and edit bound turns in the TUI[/bold #D7AFF